Author Contributions
Robert Tjarko Lange (shared first author): Co-initiated, led the project, and contributed core ideas. Coded the experiment core of The Agentic Scientist codebase and conducted the aggregated paper generation experiments. Contributed the Learned CMA results. Led the writing of the paper.
Luca Grillotti (shared first author): Co-initiated the project and contributed core ideas. Led the development and validation of autoillustrate. Contributed system features, visualization interface and evidence generation pipeline. Conducted the RLVR and ablation experiments. Co-led the writing of the paper.
Yutaro Yamada (shared first author): Co-initiated the project and contributed core ideas. Led the ALIFE submission and paper creation process. Conducted experiments using a rubric-based approach. Contributed to manuscript writing. Work conducted while he was at Sakana AI.
Rujikorn Charakorn: Implemented the paper outline step, paper verification, and scientific claim referencing and auditing pipeline. Implemented the multi-file edit, allowing The Agentic Scientist to work inside a code repository. Contributed the Doc-to-LoRA results.
David Ha (advising): Provided overarching guidance for the research project, offering technical insight, advice, feedback, and writing. Oversaw the public communication process.
