E.1 Hyperparameters
We use a fixed benchmark configuration across the autoillustrate variants, changing only the coding-agent model, critic availability, or effort level indicated by each variant.
Table 7 summarizes the shared settings.
The original PaperBanana baseline relies on gemini-3.1-pro-preview and gemini-3-pro-image-preview (Nano Banana Pro).
For the PaperBanana “Claude + GPT Image 2” variant, similarly to our pipeline, we use Claude Opus 4.8 for the Stylist, GPT-5.5 for the Critic, and GPT Image 2 for the Visualizer.
We retain Gemini for the Retriever because its long inputs exceed Claude’s one-million-token context limit, and retain PaperBanana’s original Planner because autoillustrate has no corresponding component that accepts images as input.
