E.2 Results with Gemini-3.1-Pro as VLM judge
Table 8 reports the PaperBananaBench scores of the same generated diagrams when judged by Gemini-3.1-Pro instead of GPT-6-Astra (Table 4).
Gemini-3.1-Pro awards higher scores than GPT-6-Astra across all methods.
The ablation trends within autoillustrate are preserved, and autoillustrate still outperforms the Gemini-based PaperBanana on Overall score (50.0 vs. 46.7).
However, PaperBanana with Claude Opus 4.8 and GPT Image 2 obtains the highest Overall score (56.5) under this judge, mainly due to higher Faithfulness (53.1 vs. 43.7), whereas GPT-6-Astra ranks it last (18.3).
This discrepancy stems from PaperBanana’s raster diagrams, which frequently contain small image-generation errors, such as disconnected or dangling arrows, that GPT-6-Astra treats as faithfulness vetoes while Gemini-3.1-Pro overlooks them; Figure 22 shows an example diagram together with the Faithfulness rationales of both judges.
A likely cause of these errors is that PaperBanana renders complex, highly detailed diagrams with a prompt-only image generation model: the model receives text alone; on the other hand, the image generation model used in autoillustrate takes the rendered editable draw.io diagram as an input image.
